      "writtenOn": "2024-05-21T09:57:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I don\u0027t fully understand Pierre\u0027 design of `PartialInputs`\n\nFrom aosp/2430515, it made the `code_hash` and `auth_hash` available **before** accessing the instance.img so that they could be validated against the stored ones.\n\nThose first inputs were \"`Partial`\" as the salt (another DICE input) was then read from the instance.img; note your [review comment](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/2430515/comment/32597ec3_f66462cf/) on aosp/2430515.\n\nHaving this 2-stage approach avoided the alternative of manipulating partially-initialized structs.\n\n\u003e `PartialInputs` should encompass all the fields that are present in the DICE certificate\n\n+1 if that is now possible; note that it wouldn\u0027t need to be \"`Partial`\" anymore.",
      "parentUuid": "a38765ac_a19efc06",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 98,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 98,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "10ece5a4082baad40c13b8b5295354c0607dd79f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
